On Wed, Oct 13, 2010 at 23:27, Lindar <lindarthebard@yahoo.com> wrote:

> It's getting to the point where I/we read "proposal" as "ignore what
> I'm saying".
>
>
I was just the other day remarking privately WRT this whole topic. I was
going to summarize the remarks, but it's late and I'm lazy and don't feel
like being politic, so I'll just paste:

13:22 < treed> The whole "continuing jufra" thing on the bpfk mailing list
is pissing me off.
13:22 < treed> They're making up bullshit solutions to a problem that
doesn't exist.
13:22 < treed> But I don't really want to spend the time or energy debating
it.
13:24 < treed> It's bullshit.
13:24 < treed> "But, how do you know when someone's continuing someone
else's jufra"
13:24 < treed> The only reason you could actually want to do that is to be
an asshole.
13:24 < treed> otherwise just fucking use go'i and add sumti as needed
13:25 < treed> And then the implication that every lojban jufra *must*
start with an .i or it's invalid.
13:26 < treed> The thing that annoys me most is the feeling that if I
don't bother with them, this kind of shit will sneak into the language.
13:26 < treed> This is really just a magnified version of what I've
been feeling for a while.
13:27 < treed> And why I dislike dealing with newbs so much these days.
13:27 < treed> And don't pay attention to the mailing lists.
13:27 < treed> It's just an endless parade of the same old shit.
13:27 < treed> I'm past wanting to tinker with the language. I'd like to
just be able to use it and not have to worry that some asshat's going to
come along and dick with my shit.
13:28 < treed> If it weren't for outstanding broken bullshit, I'd just
suggest that we declare the time for tinkering over.
13:29 < treed> And ignore the tinkerers henceforth.

